# Belt-and-braces. The deploy should point at dist/, which only ever contains
# the files build.py explicitly copies — but if the assets directory is ever
# set back to the repo root, these must not be published.
#
# This matters: a deploy from the repo root uploads .git, which publishes the
# entire commit history to anyone who asks for it.

.git
.github
.wrangler
.writeup
dist

content
*.py
.python-version
README.md
.gitignore
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
